{"title":"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equiangular convex hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/623d650de934c2336d699b709f39ca7a9cc38dc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 1, BC = 4, CD = 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"207\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b8134ee3d6f18f17648fd22da87c9531d7cd6e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = 4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> The area of the hexagon is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7159eb56618c91651387fc9ab5b69b32e9a0e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\frac {15}2\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }9\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ }16 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }\\frac{39}4\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\frac{43}4\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"488\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Equiangularity means that each internal angle must be exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fd424e953ac76b50bf6103875acc049d21d3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />.\nThe information given by the problem statement looks as follows:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/c/2fcaeaff120ed09924376ada47cd9c2603a51efc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); pair O=(0,0), E=dir(0), NE=dir(60), NW=dir(120); draw(O -- (O+E) -- (O+E+4*NE) -- (O+E+4*NE+2*NW) -- (O-3*E+4*NE+2*NW)); dot(O); dot(O+E); dot(O+E+4*NE); dot(O+E+4*NE+2*NW); dot(O-3*E+4*NE+2*NW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,O,SW);  label(&quot;$B$&quot;,O+E,SE);  label(&quot;$C$&quot;,O+E+4*NE,E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,O+E+4*NE+2*NW,NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,O-3*E+4*NE+2*NW,NW); [/asy]\" width=\"162\" height=\"165\" /></center>\n<p>We can now place this incomplete polygon onto a triangular grid, finish it, compute its area in unit triangles, and multiply the result by the area of the unit triangle.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c7f5471656c5757d32fd94b3554f8d4a6eb3b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); pair O=(0,0), E=dir(0), NE=dir(60), NW=dir(120); draw(O -- (O+E) -- (O+E+4*NE) -- (O+E+4*NE+2*NW) -- (O-3*E+4*NE+2*NW) -- (O-3*E+3*NE+2*NW) -- cycle, 0.8red+4bp);  for (int i=-5; i&lt;=1; ++i) { draw( (O+i*E-1.5*NE)--(O+i*E+6.5*NE), dashed ); } for (int i=-2; i&lt;=5; ++i) { draw( (O+i*E-1.5*NW)--(O+i*E+6.5*NW), dashed ); } for (int i=-1; i&lt;=6; ++i) { draw( (O-2.5*E+i*NW)--(O+5.5*E+i*NW), dashed ); }   dot(O); dot(O+E); dot(O+E+4*NE); dot(O+E+4*NE+2*NW); dot(O-3*E+4*NE+2*NW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,O,SW);  label(&quot;$B$&quot;,O+E,SE);  label(&quot;$C$&quot;,O+E+4*NE,E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,O+E+4*NE+2*NW,NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,O-3*E+4*NE+2*NW,NW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(O-3*E+3*NE+2*NW),W); [/asy]\" width=\"282\" height=\"178\" /></center>\n<p>We see that the figure contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/8/c38d81afc2fb4328ead7dde7d51221bdbac7bc53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> unit triangles, and therefore its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/2/102657122794c5dc510a82a151894c937177671c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{43\\sqrt{3}}4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99fc333e1f38c877f7f5a3e7106c604f85126488.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); draw((0,0)--(7,12.124)--(14,0)--cycle); draw((6,10.392)--(8,10.392)); draw((10,0)--(12,3.464)); draw((1,1.732)--(2,0)); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,(7,13),S); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;,(14,0),S); label(&quot;$Z$&quot;,(0,0),S); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(6,10.392),W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(8,10.392),E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(12,3.464),E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(10,0),S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(2,0),S); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(1,1.732),W); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(7,12.124)--(8,10.392),NE); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(6,10.392)--(8,10.392),S); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(8,10.392)--(12,3.464),NE); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(10,0)--(12,3.464),NW); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(14,0)--(12,3.464),NE); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(1,1.732)--(2,0),NE); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(0,0)--(2,0),S); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(0,0)--(1,1.732),NW); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(6,10.392)--(7,12.124),NW); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(10,0)--(14,0),S); [/asy]\" width=\"352\" height=\"328\" /></center>\n<p>An equiangular hexagon can be made by drawing an equilateral triangle and cutting out smaller triangles from the corners. \nLabeling the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bbdddc14ceb6746168d9e95100b12ba8c9a7493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X Y$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> and drawing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> of length one will remove one equilateral triangle of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and drawing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> will take out another equilateral triangle of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.Labeling the other sides of the smaller equilateral triangles, we can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />, or the side length of the equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Now, because we know what the side length of the triangle is, what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/521eb037ef25ecef93c9644d789eed0163a05c52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DY$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is, and it is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b6e51503abd50280c5d6703c03da6cfd2b0691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59e9072f1b1ea142e11dd0e2e125c5663915b31d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7-4-2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"12\" />. Now, to calculate the area of the hexagon we can simply subtract the area of the smaller equilateral triangles from the larger equilateral triangle. The areas of the smaller equilateral triangles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4f1fec83f7bd58c6da9f9ed94b95cac78f8af8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\implies\\frac{1\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"41\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f61dbb955476c2f518c2a0f2d41b90dbc0325d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\implies\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\implies\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"205\" height=\"41\" /> and the area of the large equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edb2eb40590173ec2ee84aec469bd3a4d98e104f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\implies\\frac{49\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"41\" /> so the area of the hexagon would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b05b0655b24d87798f89c8e7d91843ab20356846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{49\\sqrt{3}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt {3}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}-\\sqrt{3}\\implies\\boxed{\\frac{43\\sqrt{3}}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"301\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME\" title=\"1999 AHSME\">1999 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192144\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.090 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 209/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7024/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.204      1 -total\n 58.26%    7.110      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 39.23%    4.787      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7638:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017192144 and revision id 224558. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}